# Frontend rules

## Components

- Every UI surface is a Nuxt component in `app/components/` (Sidebar, AppHeader, CommitGraph, etc.).
- Reuse `XTerm.vue` for any embedded terminal — do not duplicate xterm/WebSocket logic.
- Commit graph layout lives in `app/utils/graph.ts`; keep SVG rendering in `CommitGraph.vue`.

## State (Pinia)

| Store | Role |
|-------|------|
| `projects` | Sidebar list, selected project, add/remove |
| `repo` | Git data for active project (log, branches, status, staging) |
| `ui` | Terminal open, GitHub setup modal |

Load repo data when `projects.selected.path` changes (`app/app.vue` watcher).

## Styling

- Themes are CSS variables in `app/assets/css/main.css` (`[data-theme=…]`, 4 dark + 2 light). Tailwind's `white`, `slate-100…600`, `red|green|amber|blue-200…400`, `ink-*`, `accent`, `accent-strong`, `on-accent`, `ink-line` map to them — so use those utilities, never hex colours.
- Text on `bg-accent` → `text-on-accent`; accent text on an accent tint → `text-accent-strong`; input/checkbox borders → `border-ink-line`.
- Every token pair is WCAG AA contrast-checked; adding a theme means adding a full block of variables.
- Utility classes: `.btn-primary`, `.btn-ghost`, `.btn-subtle`, `.input` in `app/assets/css/main.css`.
- No inline style sprawl — prefer Tailwind utilities.

## Dialogs

- Never use `window.alert` / `confirm` / `prompt`: the Tauri app's WKWebView doesn't implement them (alert shows nothing, confirm returns `false`, prompt returns `null`).
- Use `appAlert`, `appConfirm`, `appPrompt`, `alertError` (`app/composables/useDialog.ts`), rendered by `AppDialog.vue`.

## API calls

- Use `$fetch` to `/api/git/*`, `/api/projects/*`, `/api/gh/*`.
- WIP / uncommitted row uses `WIP` constant from `stores/repo.ts`.
